WEBVTT

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.150
You have my permission to use Zicterium.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.850
Purge the vampires!

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.450
<i>I have to stop this...</i>

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.610
I only wish it had all been a dream...

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:08.890
Negotiated Solution

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.900
Last week's train explosion 
is being reported

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:13.480
as a terrorist act carried out by 
Victor Frankenstein and his gang.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.480
That would be Finis's doing.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.850
Well, no matter.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.670
Anyway, it seems Finis desperately 
wants that monster.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.810
You said you saw her, 
did you not, Leonhardt?

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.450
I did.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.030
I am interested.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.000
If I could get my hands on that monster,

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.160
what would happen to the 
look on that boy's face?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.900
So we're all on the wanted list, huh?

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.680
What to do about this?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.320
If we leave London, 
most would stop chasing us,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.070
but we can't achieve our goal that way.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.630
That's true. Jeez...

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.540
The town's all hyped up for 
the knighting ceremony,

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.090
and we can't even enjoy the festivities.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.880
Don't make that face.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.150
Saint's already taking action.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.330
He'll figure out something we can do.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.050
Okay...

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.780
Sorry for the wait.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.790
Lunch is ready... Hey!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.040
Sisi! Not that part!

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.510
Jeez... Are all my other 
missing parts his victims, too?

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.290
You just can't keep all 
your junk tidied up.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.510
Huh?! Th-That's not true!

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.510
Is Fran all right?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.050
He hasn't eaten since yesterday.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.040
He's been locked up in his lab.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.420
Maybe being marked as the 
principal offender is bugging him.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.030
I doubt that.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:48.050
Fran once had the confidence 
of Queen Victoria.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.400
I'm sure he has some things on 
his mind after what's happened.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.350
Fran...

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.710
Thanks for going to the trouble.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.280
Once I start my experiments, 
I get too focused.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.560
I forgot to eat.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.860
You should rest a little.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.590
You always work so hard for us.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.680
Oh, no...

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.070
It's okay. I'm someone you should resent.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.280
What about you? You seem down.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.010
I'm confused.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.070
About Finis being my younger brother...

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.770
He said he knew about the Horologium,
 and about my father.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:46.340
What is Finis trying to do?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.330
Don't worry.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.730
You can trust Lupin.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.470
Van and the Count will protect 
you if necessary, too.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.800
Oh, and Impey too, of course.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.950
You're also very dependable, Fran.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.990
I'll try my best to be 
of use to all of you.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.500
Cardia...

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.760
That's right.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.500
For all of us.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.480
Did you hear about the prize for the race?

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:30.630
Yeah, they say it's something that 
belonged to the modern-day Prometheus.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.640
"I've heard what's going on."

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.920
"I'll lend you a hand anytime you need."

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.780
That's the message I was told to relay.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.660
There'll be no need for that.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:59.970
They are not the types to 
be apprehended so easily.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:23.930
Fran?

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.830
You're...

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.490
Hold it!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.170
Stop!

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.990
Sorry, but I need to borrow your clothes.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.260
Where's the other one?

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.640
You!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.540
C-Cardia?!

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.810
Why—

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:07.130
I saw you leave, so I followed you.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.760
Followed me? But...

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.680
Wh-What are you doing?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.770
You need his clothes, right?

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.370
Yeah, but...

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.400
Wait, that's not the point!

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.510
You know you shouldn't be here.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.690
The others will be worried.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.520
The same goes for you.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:25.170
Where are you going?

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.720
Where am I...

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.560
I'm heading to Buckingham Palace.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.750
I'm going to get our wanted status revoked.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.040
I'll negotiate with Victoria.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:39.620
Negotiate?

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.130
We need to run for now!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.370
Let's hide here and keep an 
eye on things for a while.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.810
I'm worried about you, Fran.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.920
I'm fine. This is something I need to do.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.650
If we make it back safe...

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.760
I know.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.410
I'd like to sleep to my heart's content.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.630
And...

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.170
I'll get Impey to cook us a feast.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.700
We'll all shop for ingredients together.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.670
Here. It's your turn next.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.360
What do you want to do?

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.220
Lupin asked me the same thing.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.600
He asked if I had a wish.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:32.850
And?

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:36.150
I want to feel warmth, too.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.540
I want to touch it with my hands.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.200
But I can't.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:51.130
So long as I have this 
poison, it's impossible.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.130
Your poison...

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.640
I—

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:04.150
I am Rempart Leonhardt of the British Army.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:07.510
Victor Frankenstein, you and your gang

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.400
are to surrender graciously!

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.310
How did they find us?

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.140
Twilight!

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:25.170
I'll protect you. Trust me.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.670
After them! Follow me!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.300
Cardia!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.530
I won't harm you.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.010
I've been ordered to 
bring you back with me.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.610
As fellow servants of England,

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
I ask you to stand down.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.980
Cardia, now's our chance.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.510
Wh-What is this?!

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:06.520
You got the jump on the 
gentleman thief. Not bad.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.590
I came to help you two.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.090
Lupin, why are you here?

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:15.520
We don't have time to chat.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:20.040
Run!

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:25.110
Fran, you disappeared right 
before the knighting ceremony.

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.390
I figured you were probably 
planning to try something.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:32.410
We were right to track 
the army's movements.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.340
Clever, as usual.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.170
Lupin?

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.430
Impey's waiting up ahead.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:39.750
Run to him!

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:41.360
But what about you two?

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.520
There aren't enough of them to worry about.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.050
Thanks.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.510
Now, then...

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:54.430
Your opponents are the 
gentleman thief and his henchman.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.480
Don't think you'll get to 
leave here unscathed.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.650
Who're you calling a henchman?

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:06.440
Impey!

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:09.900
You're here!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.910
I've missed you, Cardia!

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:15.910
Can this thing carry three?

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.790
It can now. I've improved it.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.180
It takes a little time 
to fire up, though...

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.790
Professor Stein! I can't let you escape!

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:26.310
Impey, hurry!

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.140
I know, I know.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:40.950
Yes! We've taken flight into the vast sky!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.540
Van! We're getting out of here, too!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:48.740
Hold it!

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.240
So, where're we headed?

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:56.850
Buckingham Palace.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.260
Okay, then. The palace it is.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.750
Wait! The palace?!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.720
After I get out, I want you 
to escape with Cardia.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.220
H-Huh?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.920
Fran, you're really going alone?

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:12.390
I figured that huge thing would be here.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.520
Huh?!

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.400
They're shooting in the 
middle of the city?!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.870
Impey! Evade them and get to the palace!

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.060
That's gonna be really hard!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.910
Damn it! We're desperate now!

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:40.620
All right!

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:41.630
I see it!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.400
Buckingham Palace!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:47.790
Oh, crap!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.060
Hey, what is that?

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.380
Successful landing?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.200
Well, we managed to get—

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.460
into trouble!

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.460
You're the wanted criminals, aren't you?!

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.080
Don't move!

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.580
I've rigged bombs all over the grounds!

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:26.390
Fran?

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:35.970
Try anything funny and everyone 
here gets blown to bits!

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:38.770
Victoria!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.340
I need to talk to you! 
Send your soldiers away!

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.280
Good. Now don't make a move.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.300
Fran...

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.390
It's okay. Wait right here.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:58.660
It's been a long time, Professor Stein.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.050
This has turned into quite 
the romantic reunion.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:04.680
If you don't want this place to explode,

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:09.010
revoke our wanted status immediately 
and guarantee our safety.

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:13.560
Swear you won't hold us responsible 
for the recent disturbance.

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:21.440
You mean to threaten me, the one who stands 
at the top of the British Empire?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.810
That isn't like you.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.690
Have those friends of yours influenced you?

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.330
She's scary! Is this really gonna work?

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:32.440
What a pretty girl. Almost like... Yes,

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:35.280
like a manmade doll.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.850
She has nothing to do with this!

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:42.700
All you need to do is accept my demands.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:48.060
You think a silly toy like that

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:52.970
can fool me, Alexandrina Victoria?

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.470
You're a terrible negotiator.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:15:59.620
No!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.390
Cardia, don't! It's dangerous!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.220
Fran!

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:05.600
Liquid explosive.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.610
If this hits the ground, you and I

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.620
are both dead.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.970
I've taken steps to ensure 
that the information

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:17.070
you want on Zicterium will spread 
to other countries if I die.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:22.870
That's the scenario you 
fear the most, isn't it?

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:30.520
It appears you're telling 
the truth this time.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:35.000
And I had such high hopes for you. 
How could you treat me this way?

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.790
You're the one who betrayed me!

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:42.140
You want to use Zicterium 
in the Vampire War?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.730
This country is surrounded by major powers.

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:48.500
There's no telling when 
one might attack us.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:54.220
Our only hope to prevent that is to show 
them our overwhelming military might.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.480
<i>I can still stop this... 
There's still time.</i>

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:05.900
No...

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.180
This wasn't supposed to happen...

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:12.480
I...

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.770
I never meant to create any weapons.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:19.300
For everyone in this country... I wanted...

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.300
Choose now, Victoria.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:35.030
Die with me here and let that knowledge 
spread throughout the world,

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.520
or set us free.

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:59.050
My beloved citizens,

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:05.980
it has just been proven that 
all the charges brought against

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.560
Victor Frankenstein and his gang are false.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.820
Upon my crown,

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.310
I guarantee their safety.

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:19.020
Any who harm them will be considered 
an enemy of the British Empire.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.270
Professor Stein.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:27.340
I will grant you this victory out of 
respect for your strong resolve.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:31.530
However, I advise you against angering me.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.050
Fran...

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.230
There's something I want you all to know.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:57.230
I was once involved in a certain 
project as an alchemist.

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:02.250
It was a project to create 
the Philosopher's Stone.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.070
The Philosopher's Stone?

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.630
The thing that can turn junk into gold

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.110
and give people eternal life?

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.770
Isn't that just a legend, though?

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:14.750
No one could make one.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.470
Right. There was no way we could make one.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:22.260
But at the time, I believed I could.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:25.520
So I tried it, and as a result,

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.190
I created something terrifying.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.760
It was called Zicterium.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:36.640
A devilish poison used to massacre 
vampires in the war two years ago.

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.770
You mean...

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:44.820
Isaac himself took over 
the project after that.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.250
Isaac?!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:51.760
And he created something 
else from the Zicterium.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.910
It was the Horologium.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:59.960
After witnessing the poison 
I created being used as a weapon,

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.100
I fled. I was terrified.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:05.250
I'm sorry I didn't say anything.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:09.920
Cardia, all the agony you've 
experienced is my fault.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:13.950
If I hadn't created that 
poison, you wouldn't...

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:23.860
But it's thanks to the 
Horologium that I'm alive.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.440
I can enjoy being with you all.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.020
It feels warm.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.750
That makes me happy.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.460
It's thanks to you that I'm here.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.330
Thank you, Fran.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:55.370
Thank you, Cardia.

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:05.750
Smiling suits you, 
just like any other girl.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.210
I swear to you, Cardia,

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.730
that I'll get rid of the 
poison in you someday.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:15.690
Your wish isn't impossible at all.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.750
Let me prove that to you.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:26.000
<i>I had given up so long ago 
on touching anyone,</i>

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.580
<i>on dreaming like a normal person.</i>

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:32.620
<i>Right now, none of those 
wishes can come true,</i>

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.930
<i>but can I really continue to wish for them?</i>

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:11.460
To our freedom!

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:15.580
How many toasts have you made now?

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:18.320
This should make it a bit easier to work.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:22.400
Isaac had his own research facility.

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:25.950
If we can just find it, 
we can move forward...

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:27.750
We might yet find out.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:29.140
Saint?

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:31.020
Did you find something?

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:31.890
Yes.

00:23:32.350 --> 00:23:35.250
Now it's all up to his efforts.
